WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:01.134
Tonight, former President

00:00:01.134 --> 00:00:02.502
Donald Trump is heading to Rapid City,

00:00:02.502 --> 00:00:03.403
South Dakota.

00:00:03.403 --> 00:00:04.537
This marks his first public

00:00:04.537 --> 00:00:05.872
rally since he was indicted

00:00:05.872 --> 00:00:06.573
in Fulton County,

00:00:06.573 --> 00:00:07.674
Georgia, on charges

00:00:07.674 --> 00:00:09.843
related to overturning the last election.

00:00:09.843 --> 00:00:11.111
Lest we forget, the last time

00:00:11.111 --> 00:00:12.645
Trump was in South Dakota,

00:00:12.645 --> 00:00:13.380
Governor Kristi

00:00:13.380 --> 00:00:14.147
Noem offered him

00:00:14.147 --> 00:00:15.448
a very nice miniature

00:00:15.448 --> 00:00:18.118
replica of Mount Rushmore with Mr.

00:00:18.118 --> 00:00:18.952
Trump's face on it.

00:00:18.952 --> 00:00:21.388
This time, the governor may offer him

00:00:21.388 --> 00:00:22.956
a presidential endorsement.

00:00:22.956 --> 00:00:24.457
CNN's Kyung Lah is in Rapid City,

00:00:24.457 --> 00:00:25.492
South Dakota.

00:00:25.492 --> 00:00:26.359
Governor Noem,

00:00:26.359 --> 00:00:28.728
very popular, but Trump arguably doesn't

00:00:28.728 --> 00:00:30.296
need her endorsement. Right.

00:00:30.296 --> 00:00:32.065
The fundamental right.

00:00:32.065 --> 00:00:33.466
He doesn't necessarily

00:00:33.466 --> 00:00:36.302
what this may be all about this evening

00:00:36.302 --> 00:00:37.670
with CNN reporting

00:00:37.670 --> 00:00:38.371
that Governor

00:00:38.371 --> 00:00:40.407
Noem is expected to endorse him

00:00:40.407 --> 00:00:41.274
this evening here.

00:00:41.274 --> 00:00:43.143
Rapid City, South Dakota, state

00:00:43.143 --> 00:00:45.612
that Republicans won by a very large

00:00:45.612 --> 00:00:47.747
margin is more of a job interview.

00:00:47.781 --> 00:00:49.382
He hasn't picked a vice president

00:00:49.382 --> 00:00:50.116
yet, Jake.

00:00:50.116 --> 00:00:52.185
And that really is what we're expecting

00:00:52.185 --> 00:00:52.752
to see tonight,

00:00:52.752 --> 00:00:53.486
an undercurrent

00:00:53.486 --> 00:00:55.622
of a job application of sorts, Jake.

00:00:55.889 --> 00:00:57.090
And Trump is known

00:00:57.090 --> 00:00:59.192
for spending his time at rallies, sharing

00:00:59.793 --> 00:01:01.828
sharing his various grievances.

00:01:01.828 --> 00:01:03.663
Are we expecting him to introduce

00:01:03.663 --> 00:01:05.799
any new policies this evening to

00:01:05.899 --> 00:01:08.935
to help the American people as we see

00:01:09.636 --> 00:01:11.371
Well, in short, no.

00:01:11.371 --> 00:01:12.639
And there might be a reason

00:01:12.639 --> 00:01:13.740
why he doesn't feel

00:01:13.740 --> 00:01:15.608
he necessarily has to.

00:01:15.608 --> 00:01:17.243
We spend some time talking to people

00:01:17.243 --> 00:01:19.179
who were coming into this theater

00:01:19.179 --> 00:01:20.580
to ask them what they want to hear.

00:01:20.580 --> 00:01:22.282
What policies do you want?

00:01:22.282 --> 00:01:23.149
One woman did say

00:01:23.149 --> 00:01:25.018
she wants him to address inflation,

00:01:25.018 --> 00:01:26.186
but she doesn't expect

00:01:26.186 --> 00:01:27.821
any policy to come out of it

00:01:27.821 --> 00:01:28.855
this evening.

00:01:28.855 --> 00:01:30.423
What they want to hear from

00:01:30.423 --> 00:01:31.558
him is the fight.

00:01:31.558 --> 00:01:32.192
There are people

00:01:32.192 --> 00:01:33.660
who are wearing his mug shot

00:01:33.660 --> 00:01:34.661
from Fulton County.

00:01:34.661 --> 00:01:36.896
I want you to listen to what they told us

00:01:37.297 --> 00:01:38.064
when the president

00:01:39.265 --> 00:01:39.632
This is

00:01:39.632 --> 00:01:40.633
a picture of Trump

00:01:40.633 --> 00:01:43.002
at his finest, being defiant

00:01:43.837 --> 00:01:46.406
against the establishment

00:01:46.406 --> 00:01:48.508
that is trying to take him down

00:01:48.608 --> 00:01:50.777
in a political season.

00:01:50.777 --> 00:01:54.481
Depends whose lie you're talking about.

00:01:54.481 --> 00:01:56.382
You've got the court system

00:01:56.382 --> 00:01:59.552
that is changing quite a bit

00:01:59.552 --> 00:02:01.921
because they're what they state

00:02:04.791 --> 00:02:05.492
is.

00:02:05.492 --> 00:02:06.593
No, nothing.

00:02:06.759 --> 00:02:07.494
Let's just say

00:02:07.494 --> 00:02:10.196
it's a fight between good and evil.

00:02:11.431 --> 00:02:13.233
And a lot of what's been happening

00:02:13.233 --> 00:02:14.434
is evil.

00:02:14.801 --> 00:02:16.836
He's bringing out the good.

00:02:17.237 --> 00:02:19.305
I think he he looks out for his people.

00:02:19.305 --> 00:02:21.774
I think he cares about us.

00:02:24.310 --> 00:02:25.645
So what we'll be listening

00:02:25.645 --> 00:02:27.113
for, Jake, is whether or not

00:02:27.113 --> 00:02:27.514
the former

00:02:27.514 --> 00:02:28.515
president addresses

00:02:28.515 --> 00:02:29.549
any recent news,

00:02:29.549 --> 00:02:30.517
especially today's news

00:02:30.517 --> 00:02:31.718
out of Fulton County.

00:02:31.718 --> 00:02:33.219
But as far as policy.

00:02:33.219 --> 00:02:34.454
Not so much.

00:02:34.454 --> 00:02:34.787
All right.

00:02:34.787 --> 00:02:36.823
Kyung Lah in Rapid City, South Dakota,

00:02:36.823 --> 00:02:37.457
thanks so much.

